          "date": "2026-10-27 06:29:59.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-21042 ldlm: revoke export locks with a blocking AST",
        "message": "LU-21042 ldlm: revoke export locks with a blocking AST\n\nldlm_revoke_export_locks() is called on nodemap changes to make\nclients drop cached permissions.  It cancelled the locks of the\nexport on the server only, as if the client had been evicted, so\nthe client kept its locks and its cached dentries and attributes.\nLater changes by other clients or through another MDT no longer sent\na blocking AST to the client, and it would use stale data.  E.g.\nafter sanity-hsm test_411 changed a nodemap, test_500 would create a\ndirectory on a remote MDT, and then stat would return -ENOENT from a\nstale negative dentry.\n\nSend a blocking AST for each granted IBITS and EXTENT lock of the\nexport instead, so the client cancels the locks and drops its cache.\nA client that does not cancel is evicted by the lock callback\ntimeout.  Flock and group locks are not revoked.\n\nThe nodemap code calls ldlm_revoke_export_locks() with nodemap locks\nheld, so it must not wait for client replies.  Queue the export with\na reference to the ldlm_bl threads instead, which take the locks from\nexp_lock_hash and send the ASTs.  An export that is already queued is\nnot queued again, and an export that is evicted or disconnected\nbefore the revoke runs is skipped, since its locks are cancelled\nwithout ASTs.  nodemap_modify and other nodemap changes return before\nthe revocation is complete.\n\nThe revoke ASTs are still sent synchronously from the ldlm_bl thread,\nwhich waits for the replies, so a dead client holds that thread until\nit is evicted.  Limit revoke work to about half of the maximum number\nof ldlm_bl threads, so that dead clients cannot tie up the pool\nneeded for evictions and other blocking callbacks.  Sending the ASTs\nasynchronously through ptlrpcd is left for later, since\nldlm_cb_interpret() would need an lu_env there.\n\nExtend sanity-sec test_82 to check that a nodemap change makes the\nclient cancel its MDT0000 locks without an eviction.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-sec\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanity-hsm\nFixes: 64a0a6c4559b (\"LU-19157 nodemap: revoke export locks on nodemap change\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I271021c58f6ae916c10ca3d0f37683a0503ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
